urce_search_partial":[],"original_representation":[{"custody_records_in":["clause-drafts","fr-originals","later-events"],"fr_citation":"44 FR 30311","from":"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output","grade":"fr_originals_high","location_confidence":"high","publication_date":"1979-05-25","ref":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"signing_date":"1979-05-23","source_id":"fr-originals:EO:12139:fc40849c0896","strong":true,"text_path":"texts/EO_12139.txt","why":"page location high; location_verified is false - open the PDF pages"}],"savings_leads":[],"whole_order_end":[],"whole_order_end_total":0},"provisional_status":"yes","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"confirm","counterevidence":"confirm","ending_or_current_basis":"research","opus_media":"research","original_text":"confirm","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":["ending_or_current_basis","opus_media"],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1979-05-23","later-events_catalog":"1979-05-23","stage19_causal_queue":"1979-05-23"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:12139","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-101. Pursuant to Section 102(a)(1) of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance \nA ct of 1978 (50 U.S.C. 1802(a)), the A ttorney G eneral is authorized to approve \nelectronic surveillance to acquire foreign intelligence inform ation w ithout a \ncourt order, but only if the A ttorney G eneral m akes the certifications required \nby that Section.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-101","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-101","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-102. Pursuant to Section 102(b) of the Foreign Intelligence A ct of 1978 (50\nU.S.C. 1802(b)), the A ttorney G eneral is authorized to approve applications to \nthe court having jurisdiction under Section 103 of that A ct to obtain orders for \nelectronic surveillance for the purpose of obtaining foreign intelligence infor­\nm ation.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-102","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-102","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-103. Pursuant to Section 104(a)(7) of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance \nA ct of 1978 (50 U.S.C. 1804(a)(7)), the follow ing officials, each of whom is \nem ployed in the area of national security or defense, is designated to m ake the \ncertifications required by Section 104(a)(7) of the A ct in support of applica­\ntions to conduct electronic surveillance:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-103 (lead-in)","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-103","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Secretary of State.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-103(a)","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-103(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Secretary of Defense.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-103(b)","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-103(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Director of Central Intelligence.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-103(c)","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-103(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) Director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-103(d)","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-103(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(e) Deputy Secretary of State.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-103(e)","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-103(e)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(f) Deputy Secretary of Defense.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-103(f)","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-103(f)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(g) Deputy Director of Central Intelligence.\nNone of the above officials, nor anyone officially acting in that capacity, may  \nexercise the authority to make the above certifications, unless that official has  \nbeen appointed by the President with the advice and consent of the Senate.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-103(g)","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-103(g)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-104. Section 2-202 of Executive O rder No. 12036 is am ended by inserting the \nfollow ing at the end of that section: “A ny electronic surveillance, as defined in \nthe Foreign Intelligence Surveillance A ct of 1978, shall be conducted in \naccord ance w ith that A ct as w ell as this O rder.”.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-104","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-104","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-105. Section 2-203 of Executive Order No. 12036 is amended by inserting the  \nfollowing at the end of that section: “Any monitoring which constitutes  \nelectronic surveillance as defined in the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act  \nof 1978 shall be conducted in accordance with that Act as well as this Order.”.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13; Sec. 1-105","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12139#sec1-105","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 30311, PDF pages 11-13","sha256":"fc40849c0896aa6e1673d93a9746d8e8c08364eb1df142d177c2a54bc00dad8f","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-05-25/pdf/FR-1979-05-25.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 12 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: current legal basis not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"yes"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:12139"}
